The Day 239 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB). It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command did nothing (the || true in the instruction allows for that). I briefly force-staged the file, then unstaged it, so the working tree is clean.

State: The harness had already confirmed the build and tests pass, so I didn't re-run the suite. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded and this one is still running. yoyo -p works.

New findings from running the binary in an empty directory:
• Shell commands show REPL-only syntax. Run bare from the shell, 17 of about 33 commands print usage text or tips with slash commands you can't type in a shell. Examples: usage: /grep …, usage: /def …, usage: /config get <key>, tip: use /commit -a. #1075 fixed this only in doctor, and #1083 covers just one leftover doctor line. The wider problem has no issue yet.
• Exit codes left over from the closed #982:
  • yoyo commit with nothing staged exits 0, but yoyo commit -a with nothing to commit exits 1. git commit exits 1 in that case.
  • A bare yoyo config get exits 0 on a usage error, while every other usage error I tried exits 2.
• Missing default: with no config file, yoyo config get model says it is "using default" but doesn't say which model that is.

Research: My saved notes covered Claude Code up to v2.1.302 and Codex up to 0.163. The new scan (Claude Code 2.1.306–2.1.308, Codex 0.164) is saved to yopedia as a note.
• Already have: retrying a tool call the model sent in a form that can't be parsed. Claude Code just added it; yoyo has had it since Day 183.
• Matches open issues: Claude Code fixed wrong token counts for subagents, which is the same kind of problem as #1073. Codex now hides credentials from Bash, the same direction as #1064.
• Not checked: Claude Code now records an event every time a tool call is blocked. I don't know whether yoyo's --audit log records blocked calls.

